<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
	<head>
    <% include ../partials/head %>
	 <meta charset="utf-8" />
	 <meta name="description" content="Projectile motion simulation example. An interactive animation created using Easy JavaScript Simulation 
	 (EJSS) showing the parabolic trajectory of an object." />

	<meta name="keywords" content="projectile motion simulation,EJSS example,Easy JavaScript Simulation,
	HtmlView EJSS,variables in EJSS,EJSS console,initial velocity,angle in degrees and radians,velocity components x y,
	Evolution page EJSS,2D motion,parabolic path,physics simulation,2D Shape,Drawable elements,EJSS tutorial" />

	</head>
    <body>
	<div class="content-wrapper">
	<div class="row">
	<div class="col-xs-12 col-md-12 col-lg-12">
        <header>
			<% include ../partials/header %>
		</header>
        </div>
		</div>
		<div class="row">
    <div class="naslov col-xs-12 col-md-12 col-lg-12">
        <h1>Example of Creating a Projectile Motion App in EJSS</h1>
    </div>
    <hr>
</div>

<!--div class="row">
    <p class="col-xs-12 col-md-12 col-lg-12" style="height:300px;text-align: center;">
        Website under construction...
    </p>
</div-->

<div class="row">
    <p class="col-xs-12 col-md-12 col-lg-12">
        Let's start the EJS console and run the JavaScript version of EJS.
    </p>

    <p class="col-xs-12 col-md-12 col-lg-12">
        <img class="slike_u_tekstu" src="images/upotrebaEjsaOpis/kosHitacOEjsu/Pocetni ekran1.png"
        alt="Creating a model in EJSS, Start screen" />
    </p>

    <p class="col-xs-12 col-md-12 col-lg-12">
        At the top of the window, there are tabs: Description, Model, and HtmlView.
        In the Description tab, you can add a description by double-clicking the page. In the Model tab, you define variables and functions,
        and in HtmlView, you design the visual part of the application.
    </p>

    <p class="col-xs-12 col-md-12 col-lg-12">
        <img class="slike_u_tekstu" src="images/upotrebaEjsaOpis/kosHitacOEjsu/model view.png"
        alt="Creating a model in EJSS, model creation" />
    </p>

    <p class="col-xs-12 col-md-12 col-lg-12">
        In the model, we define variables, initialize them in the Initialisation section, which resets the values each time the animation restarts.
        The Evolution tab contains motion equations, and the Custom tab holds user-defined functions.
        In the Fixed Relations tab, we define equations that depend on the base ones defined in Evolution.
    </p>
</div>

<div class="row">
    <h2>Variables</h2>
    <p class="col-xs-12 col-md-12 col-lg-12">
        For projectile motion, we need to define variables for position projections, velocity, and acceleration in both X and Y directions.
        We also define constants like g (gravitational acceleration), time t, and the time increment dt.
        Smaller values of dt provide more precise results but may slow down the animation, so an optimal value like 0.05s is recommended.
    </p>

    <p class="col-xs-12 col-md-12 col-lg-12">
        Clicking the shown window opens a small dialog where you should enter the name of the new variables tab.
        We’ll name it "variables" and later create another tab for constants.
    </p>

    <p class="col-xs-12 col-md-12 col-lg-12">
        <img class="slike_u_tekstu" src="images/upotrebaEjsaOpis/kosHitacOEjsu/Ime Taba.png"
        alt="Creating a model in EJSS, Variables tab naming" />
    </p>

    <p class="col-xs-12 col-md-12 col-lg-12">
        Let’s create some essential initial variables: time t, time change dt, body position in X and Y directions (X, Y),
        and velocity components vx and vy.
    </p>

    <p class="col-xs-12 col-md-12 col-lg-12">
        <img class="slike_u_tekstu" src="images/upotrebaEjsaOpis/kosHitacOEjsu/variable1.png"
        alt="Creating a model in EJSS, Variables" />
    </p>

    <p class="col-xs-12 col-md-12 col-lg-12">
        The table has four columns: variable name, initial value, data type (default is double), and dimension if it is an array.
    </p>

    <p class="col-xs-12 col-md-12 col-lg-12">
        For motion in X and Y directions, we need velocity components vx and vy.
        These will be calculated based on the entered initial speed v and angle of projection (angleDeg).
        The angle is input in degrees but needs to be converted to radians (angle) for calculations.
    </p>

    <p class="col-xs-12 col-md-12 col-lg-12">
        Let’s add another tab for constants. Right-click somewhere on the gray area next to the first tab title and select “create new page”.
        Name it “constants”.
    </p>

    <p class="col-xs-12 col-md-12 col-lg-12">
        <img class="slike_u_tekstu" src="images/upotrebaEjsaOpis/kosHitacOEjsu/novaStrana.png" 
        alt="Creating a new constants tab in EJSS" />
    </p>

    <p class="col-xs-12 col-md-12 col-lg-12">
        Add the constant G of type double and initialize it to 9.81.
    </p>

    <p class="col-xs-12 col-md-12 col-lg-12">
        <img class="slike_u_tekstu" src="images/upotrebaEjsaOpis/kosHitacOEjsu/Konstante.png" 
        alt="Creating constants in EJSS" />
    </p>

    <p class="col-xs-12 col-md-12 col-lg-12">
        Now let’s save the document by clicking save and naming it KosiHitac.ejss as shown:
    </p>

    <p class="col-xs-12 col-md-12 col-lg-12">
        <img class="slike_u_tekstu" src="images/upotrebaEjsaOpis/kosHitacOEjsu/Konstante.png" 
        alt="Saving the EJSS model, save dialog" />
    </p>

    <p class="col-xs-12 col-md-12 col-lg-12">
        Let’s also add another constant PI with the value 3.14.
    </p>
</div>

<div class="row">
    <h2>Initialization (Model)</h2>
    <p class="col-xs-12 col-md-12 col-lg-12">
        In this tab, we initialize all variables that should be set at the beginning of the animation.
        This section is triggered when restarting the animation. Choose Initialisation and create a new page named "initialization".
    </p>

    <p class="col-xs-12 col-md-12 col-lg-12">
        Convert the angle from degrees to radians (angle), and calculate the velocity components using that angle.
    </p>

    <p class="col-xs-12 col-md-12 col-lg-12">
        <span class="formule">vx = v * Math.cos(angle);</span>
    </p>

    <p class="col-xs-12 col-md-12 col-lg-12">
        <span class="formule">vy = v * Math.sin(angle);</span>
    </p>

    <p class="col-xs-12 col-md-12 col-lg-12">
        We used the Math class and its sine and cosine functions.
    </p>

    <p class="col-xs-12 col-md-12 col-lg-12">
        Also, set initial positions, which in this case is 0:
    </p>

    <p class="col-xs-12 col-md-12 col-lg-12">
        x = 0 and y = 0;
    </p>

    <p class="col-xs-12 col-md-12 col-lg-12">
        <img class="slike_u_tekstu" src="images/upotrebaEjsaOpis/kosHitacOEjsu/Inicijalizacija1.png" 
        alt="Creating the EJSS app. Initialization in the model" />
    </p>
</div>

<div class="row">
    <h2>Evolution (Model)</h2>
    <p class="col-xs-12 col-md-12 col-lg-12">
        Let’s create a new page in the Evolution section named “Motion”, by clicking on “Click to create page of code” at the top.
    </p>

    <p class="col-xs-12 col-md-12 col-lg-12">
        <img class="slike_u_tekstu" src="images/upotrebaEjsaOpis/kosHitacOEjsu/Evolution.png" 
        alt="Creating the EJSS app. Evolution" />
    </p>
        <div class="row">
        <h2>Evolution (model).</h2>
                <p class="col-xs-12 col-md-12 col-lg-12">
                Let’s create a new page in the Evolution section titled “Motion”, by clicking on the top part that says “Click to create page of code”.
                </p>
                <p class="col-xs-12 col-md-12 col-lg-12">
                <img class="slike_u_tekstu" src="images/upotrebaEjsaOpis/kosHitacOEjsu/Evolution.png" 
                alt="Creating an application in EJSS - Evolution" />
                </p>
                <p class="col-xs-12 col-md-12 col-lg-12">
                In this section, we define the equations of motion that determine how the variables change over time.
                </p>
                <p class="col-xs-12 col-md-12 col-lg-12">
                For projectile motion, we define the change in velocity in the Y direction due to gravity, and the change in position in both X and Y directions.
                </p>
                <p class="col-xs-12 col-md-12 col-lg-12">
                <span class="formule">vy = vy - G*dt;</span><br/>
                <span class="formule">x = x + vx*dt;</span><br/>
                <span class="formule">y = y + vy*dt;</span>
                </p>
                <p class="col-xs-12 col-md-12 col-lg-12">
                With these formulas, we simulate the motion of the object in small steps of time, defined by dt.
                </p>
        </div>

        <div class="row">
        <h2>Custom and Fixed Relations (model).</h2>
                <p class="col-xs-12 col-md-12 col-lg-12">
                In the “Custom” tab, we can define additional functions that are needed in the simulation and are created by the user.
                </p>
                <p class="col-xs-12 col-md-12 col-lg-12">
                <img class="slike_u_tekstu" src="images/upotrebaEjsaOpis/kosHitacOEjsu/custom.png" 
                alt="EJSS Custom tab - user-defined functions" />
                </p>
                <p class="col-xs-12 col-md-12 col-lg-12">
                In the “Fixed Relations” tab, we define equations that depend on the basic variables defined in the Evolution tab.
                These equations are recalculated each time the main variables change.
                </p>
        </div>

        <div class="row">
        <h2>HTML View.</h2>
                <p class="col-xs-12 col-md-12 col-lg-12">
                In the HtmlView tab, we define the visual part of the application.
                It is here that we add graphical elements, buttons, text fields, and other interface components.
                </p>
                <p class="col-xs-12 col-md-12 col-lg-12">
                For example, we can add a graph that shows the trajectory of the motion, or fields where users can input initial values.
                </p>
                <p class="col-xs-12 col-md-12 col-lg-12">
                <img class="slike_u_tekstu" src="images/upotrebaEjsaOpis/kosHitacOEjsu/HtmlView.png" 
                alt="Visual part of EJSS application - HTML View" />
                </p>
                <p class="col-xs-12 col-md-12 col-lg-12">
                Each element can be linked to a variable from the model to update in real-time during the animation.
                </p>
        </div>

        <div class="row">
        <h2>Simulation Test.</h2>
                <p class="col-xs-12 col-md-12 col-lg-12">
                After setting up the model, variables, and visual components, we can run the simulation by pressing the “Play” button.
                </p>
                <p class="col-xs-12 col-md-12 col-lg-12">
                <img class="slike_u_tekstu" src="images/upotrebaEjsaOpis/kosHitacOEjsu/RunSimulation.png" 
                alt="Running simulation in EJSS" />
                </p>
                <p class="col-xs-12 col-md-12 col-lg-12">
                The object should move along a parabolic trajectory defined by the initial speed, angle, and gravity.
                </p>
        </div>

		<div class="col-xs-12 col-md-12 col-lg-12">
        <% include ../partials/scripts %>
        <% include ../partials/footer %>
		</div>
		</div>
		</div>
	
    </body>
</html>